<div class="container">
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Features</h1>
    <p class="lede">Cueport reads a Serato library or opens a music folder with Cueport Direct, no Serato required. It analyzes local files on the Mac, lets you edit in a local working layer, and keeps library write-back behind a review.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-list">
    <article class="feature">
      <div class="feature-head">
        <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 6h6l2 2h8v10a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H4z"/><path d="M4 6v12"/><path d="M8 12h8"/><path d="M8 16h5"/></svg>
        </span>
        <h3>Serato library</h3>
      </div>
      <p>Reads crates, subcrates, tracks, BPM, key, and color labels from your local <code>_Serato_</code> folder.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature">
      <div class="feature-head">
        <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M12 3v6"/></svg>
        </span>
        <h3>Cueport Direct</h3>
      </div>
      <p>Open a music folder instead of linking Serato. Cueport builds a library from your files, no DJ software required.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature">
      <div class="feature-head">
        <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 18V7"/><path d="M8 18V5"/><path d="M12 18V10"/><path d="M16 18V8"/><path d="M20 18V6"/><path d="M4 21h16"/></svg>
        </span>
        <h3>Local audio analysis</h3>
      </div>
      <p>Cueport Direct uses <a href="https://github.com/djpardis/trailmix">trail mix</a> to compute BPM, key, waveform columns, and beatgrid markers from audio on your machine.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature">
      <div class="feature-head">
        <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polygon points="6,4 20,12 6,20"/></svg>
        </span>
        <h3>Local playback</h3>
      </div>
      <p>Play tracks from local files while browsing collections, with waveform context, cues, and beatgrid markers alongside the player.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature">
      <div class="feature-head">
        <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="7" y="2" width="10" height="20" rx="2"/><path d="M12 18h.01"/><path d="M10 6h4"/></svg>
        </span>
        <h3>iPhone companion</h3>
      </div>
      <p>Send selected collections and cached tracks to the iPhone app. Browse and play them on the go, including away from your computer.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature">
      <div class="feature-head">
        <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 18V6"/><path d="M18 18V6"/><path d="M6 12h12"/><path d="M9 9l3 3-3 3"/><path d="M14 8h4"/><path d="M14 16h4"/></svg>
        </span>
        <h3>Cue points and notes</h3>
      </div>
      <p>Read hot cues from Serato MP3 tags or create them in Cueport Direct. Add a text note to any track.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature">
      <div class="feature-head">
        <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 7h14"/><path d="M5 12h10"/><path d="M5 17h7"/><path d="M16 15l3 3"/><path d="M19 15l-3 3"/></svg>
        </span>
        <h3>Local editing layer</h3>
      </div>
      <p>Edits to cues, notes, colors, and collections are staged locally with a clear sync status on every entity.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature">
      <div class="feature-head">
        <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 20V7"/><path d="M7 12l5-5 5 5"/><path d="M5 20h14"/><path d="M5 16v4"/><path d="M19 16v4"/></svg>
        </span>
        <h3>Publish on approval</h3>
      </div>
      <p>Serato edits write back to MP3s and crate files only when you choose to publish. Cueport Direct edits remain in their own database.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature">
      <div class="feature-head">
        <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 5-3 8-7 10-4-2-7-5-7-10V6z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-5"/><path d="M8 18h8"/></svg>
        </span>
        <h3>Backups and restore points</h3>
      </div>
      <p>Serato safety copies before each publish. Cueport Direct restore points stored separately so you can roll back either source.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</div>
